#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558671} :activity/id #uuid "10f6eef1-5078-55a6-b949-5b4bf786db94" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558616 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "160b514e-c7a9-5db1-8962-33d86d078fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305342}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305342} :answer-field/id #uuid "63437be9-2066-5dad-a01a-a0e02722c169" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05184db4-a95b-5878-863f-1aa2b4e40630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305198} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1530c65-7d45-5311-814a-529b693ace24" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7aef4d9e-5adf-5d9d-be87-6231a093c423" :question/math-academy-id "q-334855" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3cf553b5-a0c0-5e03-adcb-b5e28abcb810" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558657}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558657 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "325e2bea-79c6-5d0e-86e5-ca3c08841f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t+s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557971} {:answer/id #uuid "8e624ff8-2ee1-5b70-ba81-5895a41c4248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558145} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ecf254-834a-5dbe-8b2d-44e08553fb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558228} {:answer/id #uuid "f6893209-e8c4-5a46-9f8a-822f69bcdaf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t+s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558350}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558228} :answer-field/id #uuid "dadfc882-5148-5c0c-af21-a9e418a22bd6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558464} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69fe7ba5-1b53-56bf-9a9f-f5c568562239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558069} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6829ae-e7c1-5884-afa0-116dfe94231c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558142} {:answer/id #uuid "ad7f1da6-be8e-55ae-86e2-b2f30e2b8500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558212} {:answer/id #uuid "c87fcfa6-f6e3-5441-b2a1-174c935027eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558267}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558069} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffb55f3c-2681-5734-9a74-f7bf06c53fcc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cb2daa37-d9b1-570d-9a42-38ab64cc0e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-334859" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}} </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8b6c1363-f2b6-518d-a59c-19b0d9f1d213"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558671 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59687fe-7fee-536b-ae53-62aa4e2062c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558287}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558287} :answer-field/id #uuid "bda1e7e4-3c88-5a06-909e-308c1b22da65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81eb1113-b696-53f5-ab1f-005ae9690189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc834a44-d315-5323-8d37-5104d3268aa9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a3f4d85-0623-5fd9-9cc9-8c8eac44c1ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-334846" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a7f36150-a323-543f-a05f-ad14ac2a2c6c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558616}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557852}]}
